DATA ATTRIBUTION
================

The wildfire statistics in data/ are derived from the European Forest Fire
Information System (EFFIS), part of the Copernicus Emergency Management Service,
operated by the European Commission's Joint Research Centre (JRC).

  Source file: report_2024.xlsx
  Source page: https://forest-fire.emergency.copernicus.eu/applications/data-and-services
  Licence:     Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
               https://forest-fire.emergency.copernicus.eu/about-effis/data-license
  Retrieved:   2026-07-28
  Coverage:    1980-2024, 31 countries

  © European Union, 1995-2026

CC BY 4.0 requires that changes be indicated. The following changes were made to
the source data by fetch_effis.py; no values were altered:

  1. The two worksheets were extracted to separate CSV files
     ("Burnt area (ha) 1980 - 2024" -> effis_burnt_area_ha.csv,
      "Nr. of forest fires 1980 - 2024" -> effis_number_of_fires.csv).
  2. Thousands separators, written in the source as non-breaking spaces
     (U+00A0), were removed so the values parse as numbers.
  3. Spreadsheet formatting, merged cells and styling were dropped; only cell
     values were kept.

Known limitation carried over from the source: EFFIS burnt-area mapping detects
fires of approximately 30 hectares or larger. Smaller fires are not represented
in the burnt-area figures.

The analysis, chart and all code in this repository are the author's own and are
not endorsed by or affiliated with EFFIS, Copernicus, the JRC or the European
Commission.
